                    {
                        "sense_id": "50c1a93d-8b61-3d51-8d4b-81e46e8c1b46",
                        "entry_id": "176955e0-d12b-38ef-ae45-9c6c3a8530ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Between leaves or leaf-like structures."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9643a7c1-f4c6-4415-b28a-a594a52cab13",
                                "sense_id": "50c1a93d-8b61-3d51-8d4b-81e46e8c1b46",
                                "text": "Another interesting feature in the species before us is the presence of interfoliate scars similar to those of other species of Sigillaria, especially the Tessellata and Facularia groups."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ee33061-37ed-4f38-87b4-1c05565157e0",
                                "sense_id": "50c1a93d-8b61-3d51-8d4b-81e46e8c1b46",
                                "text": "The layers are separated by gaps, the interfoliate spaces. The ensemble consituted by a layer and an interfoliate space constitutes the structural unit of clay."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "135d1e98-dc9b-4251-b254-4e10b435252d",
                                "sense_id": "50c1a93d-8b61-3d51-8d4b-81e46e8c1b46",
                                "text": "The primary fissure (arrow) and other interfoliate fissures are closed. Mild vermian volume loss and progressive chiasmatic atrophy (open arrow) are seen (B) on follow-up. The interfoliate fissures of the anterior vermian lobule, above the primary fissure (arrow), are open, whereas those below are closed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
